  "text": "Codes and Regulations for Code Compliance | Mesa County\nSkip to main content\nStage 1 Fire Restrictions enacted\nEffective beginning 12:01 a.m. Friday, Sept. 4, 2026, until further notice. These restrictions apply to all private land and BLM managed public lands within the boundaries of the Grand Junction Field Office. For more information visit the Fire Restrictions webpage.\nTranslate\nMain navigation\nMENU\nMENU\nResident Resources\nBusiness Resources\nDepartments and Services\nContact Us\nJobs\nADA\nEvents\nNews\nTranslate\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nDepartments and Services\nCommunity Development\nCode Compliance Services\nCodes and Regulations\nCodes and Regulations for Code Compliance\nCodes and regulations\nCommunity Development codes\nThe following codes and regulations govern land use within unincorporated areas of Mesa County.\nLand Development Code - 2020 (Amended 04-23-24, PDF)\nMesa County Ordinances\nLimitations on Residing on County Owned Land - Ordinance 14 (PDF)\nProhibiting the Accumulation of Rubbish - Ordinance 15 (PDF)\nPublic Health codes\nResidential Non-Agriculture Open Burning Matrix (PDF)\nInfestation and Rodent Harborage Code (PDF)\nRubbish, Refuse, and Garbage Code (PDF)\nCode Compliance Services\nContact Code Compliance\nCodes and Regulations\nComplaint Process\nResources\nContact Us\nTelephone\nDepartment Directory\nContact Information\nContact Information\nComments and Feedback\nGet in Touch\nMesa County is committed to providing equitable access to our services to the public. For accessibility assistance with any part of this website, including but not limited to any documents on this website, please visit the Mesa County ADA Compliance webpage for contact information.\n© 2026 Mesa County, Colorado\nADA Policy\nPrivacy Policy\nPowered by Interpersonal Frequency",
